MalwareLens

MalwareLens is a web-based static malware analysis platform. A user uploads a suspicious file and receives a report with its hashes, true file type, embedded indicators (URLs, IP addresses, commands), structural findings and a risk verdict. Files are only read, never executed, so analysis is safe by design.
Main features: file hashing, file type and extension-mismatch detection, indicator extraction, PE/ELF/APK inspection, entropy and packing detection, behavioral signature rules, risk scoring, AES-256 file encryption, analysis history and team sandbox communities.

